@@ -59,6 +59,15 @@ especially important when using a custom `getsizeof` function, since
 the size of an item's value will only be computed when the item is
 inserted into the cache.
 
+Use :meth:`Cache.resize` to change a cache's maximum size in place.
+If the recorded size of the retained values exceeds the new maximum,
+items are discarded using the cache's eviction policy until they fit.
+Resizing uses the sizes recorded at insertion and does not call
+:meth:`getsizeof` again for retained values.  It uses the existing
+size accounting, so floating-point rounding or overflow may leave a
+residual current size after all entries are evicted.  Resizing stops
+evicting when the cache is empty.
+
 .. note::
 
    Please be aware that all these classes are *not* thread-safe.
